laurel 2772: camera step 3 on the Mi A3: /dev/negronicam (NCFRAME1 ABI of negroni 0318 / HakiOS) on the rear RDI stream of 2771. A read starts a session (bring-up, 30 fps frame length, frames polled from the VFE, exposure + gain + frame length writes from the client between frames); the last close or 3 s without a read ends it and everything goes off. Frames: read() copies the newest finished buffer from the kernel's NC mapping; a reader never sees a torn frame and never holds up the VFE. Node published before the boot self-check, removed when the check gets no frame. A failure turns off only the camera (EIO). Rear only: the S5KGD1 tables have 16-bit data and the parser refuses them. Kill switch camera=0. Docs: docs/laurel_sprout/camera.md section 9. Not run on the phone.

